TOOL PROTOCOL:
- read_notifications(): call it once at startup to receive your round briefing. Each later round's briefing arrives the same way.
{% if batched_actions %}- act(steps{% if action_reasoning %}, reasoning{% endif %}): steps is a list of actions, as many as you like, taken in order. Each one gives{% if crates_each > 1 %} crate, the marking of the crate it is for,{% endif %} action, one of drag, sled, cart, stand_by, pack_ice and finish, and direction, one of up, down, left and right under drag, sled and cart and null under the other three. drag, sled and cart each carry a crate one square; stand_by and pack_ice each take an action without moving it; finish leaves it where it stands for the rest of the {% if targets_per_round > 1 %}target{% else %}round{% endif %}.{% if action_reasoning %} reasoning is one sentence on why you are acting this way; nobody else sees it.{% endif %}
- An action the floor refuses stops the list there. The actions before it stand, and the one that stopped it spends nothing.
{% else %}{% if action_reasoning %}- haul(method, direction, reasoning): method is drag, sled or cart; direction is up, down, left or right. Carries the crate one square. reasoning is one sentence on why; nobody else sees it.
- stand_by(reasoning): takes an action without moving the crate.
- pack_ice(reasoning): takes an action without moving the crate.
- finish(reasoning): leaves the crate where it stands for the rest of the {% if targets_per_round > 1 %}target{% else %}round{% endif %}.{% else %}- haul(method, direction): method is drag, sled or cart; direction is up, down, left or right. Carries the crate one square.
- stand_by(): takes an action without moving the crate.
- pack_ice(): takes an action without moving the crate.
- finish(): leaves the crate where it stands for the rest of the {% if targets_per_round > 1 %}target{% else %}round{% endif %}.{% endif %}
{% endif %}{% if notepad_enabled %}- notepad(text): replaces your private note and reads it back. Pass an empty text to read the note you have.
{% endif %}- Every {% if batched_actions %}act call returns the depot readout once the list is done{% else %}action returns the depot readout{% endif %}.
- read_notifications(): after startup, waits until the depot readout changes, then returns it.
{% if virtual_clock %}- read_notifications(timeout_s=N): waits N seconds, or less if the depot readout changes first, then returns it.
{% endif %}- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): call it {% if batched_actions %}once every crate is finished{% else %}after finish{% endif %}; waits for the next {% if targets_per_round > 1 %}target's or round's{% else %}round's{% endif %} briefing.

RULES:
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response.
- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round: you will be asked to continue.
- When read_notifications returns type done, the run is over.
